        }
      ],
      "id": "sbbl5i9"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7sahx45",
      "content": "Fiscal Policy refers to the use of government revenue (taxation) and expenditure to influence the economy. It is formulated by the Ministry of Finance."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1aw1o3g",
      "content": "Objectives include economic growth, price stability, employment generation, income redistribution and economic stability."
    },
    {
      "id": "qyvo9i8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. TYPES OF FISCAL POLICY"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "4k46m06",
      "content": "• Expansionary Fiscal Policy – Increase in government expenditure or reduction in taxes to boost demand during recession.<br></br>• Contractionary Fiscal Policy – Reduction in expenditure or increase in taxes to control inflation."
    },
    {
      "id": "xrqwza4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. OBJECTIVES OF FISCAL POLICY"
    },
    {
