        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "mkjw2xb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. PUBLIC DEBT"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "j81qjhz",
      "content": "Public Debt refers to total borrowings of the government to finance fiscal deficit."
    },
    {
      "type": "comparisonTable",
      "headers": [
        "Feature",
        "Direct Taxes",
        "Indirect Taxes"
      ],
      "rows": [
        [
          "Incidence & Impact",
          "Borne directly by the entity on whom it is imposed",
          "Passed on to the final consumer"
        ],
        [
          "Shiftability",
          "Tax burden cannot be shifted",
          "Tax burden can be shifted"
        ]
      ],
      "id": "cnn02wu"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yry8dxa",
      "content": "• Internal Debt – Borrowing within country<br></br>• External Debt – Borrowing from foreign sources"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 4,
      "id": "y0nxmzc",
      "content": "<strong>10.ADVANCED FISCAL CONCEPTS</strong>"
    },
    {
      "id": "ghwt0zq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. FRBM ACT – YEAR-WISE EVOLUTION & TARGETS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e421m7b",
      "content": "The Fiscal Responsibility and Budget Management (FRBM) Act was enacted in 2003 to ensure fiscal discipline and reduce fiscal deficit and public debt."
    },
    {
      "id": "wk0vz2r",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Year/Amendment</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Target</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Remarks</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>2003 (Original Act)</p>",
            "<p>Fiscal Deficit ≤ 3% of GDP</p>",
            "<p>Eliminate revenue deficit</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>2008-09</p>",
            "<p>Targets relaxed</p>",
            "<p>Global financial crisis</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>2012 Amendment</p>",
            "<p>Revised consolidation path</p>",
            "<p>Focus on effective revenue deficit</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>2018 Amendment</p>",
            "<p>Debt target 60% of GDP (40% Centre)</p>",
            "<p>FRBM Review Committee</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Post-COVID (2020-23)</p>",
            "<p>Targets temporarily relaxed</p>",
            "<p>Pandemic impact</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "fg0k4o1",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. TYPES OF TAXES"
    },
    {
      "id": "i26q7d6",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Meaning</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Example</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Progressive Tax</p>",
            "<p>Tax rate increases with income</p>",
            "<p>Income Tax</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Regressive Tax</p>",
            "<p>Tax rate decreases as income rises</p>",
            "<p>Indirect taxes impact</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Proportional Tax</p>",
            "<p>Same rate for all income levels</p>",
            "<p>Flat tax system</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "5ftj70i",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. GST STRUCTURE IN INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vmbmdg4",
      "content": "GST (Goods and Services Tax) was implemented on 1 July 2017."
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "FRBM Act (2003) evolution targets and detailed deficit comparisons are frequently tested high-value topics.",
        "Distinction between Direct and Indirect Taxes, along with the GST framework, carries high weightage in competitive exams."
      ],
      "id": "79zg4kj"
    },
    {
      "id": "5u3nhyd",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Component</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Collected By</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Applicable On</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>CGST</p>",
            "<p>Central Government</p>",
            "<p>Intra-state supply</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>SGST</p>",
            "<p>State Government</p>",
            "<p>Intra-state supply</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>IGST</p>",
            "<p>Central Government</p>",
            "<p>Inter-state supply</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "933w1tt",
      "content": "Example: If goods sold within same state → CGST + SGST.<br></br>If goods sold between two states → IGST."
    },
    {
